   "xml_index": 3,
   "xml_name": "L11_003_Mirror Images",
   "display_name": "Mirror Images",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><b>Flipping</b> a point makes its mirror image:</p>\n<ul><li>in the <b>x-axis</b> (the horizontal line): <code>(x, y)</code> becomes <code>(x, -y)</code>;</li><li>in the <b>y-axis</b> (the vertical line): <code>(x, y)</code> becomes <code>(-x, y)</code>.</li></ul>\n<div style=\"margin:6px 0 4px\"><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">p : Point</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">x = 3</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">y = 2</div></div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;padding:22px 8px 0 0;color:#8a939c\">p.flip_x() &rarr;</div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">p : Point</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">x = 3</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">y = -2</div></div></div></div>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the methods <code>flip_x()</code> and <code>flip_y()</code>, which flip the point in the x-axis and in the y-axis. They change the point and return nothing.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>p = Point(3, 2)</code> and <code>p.flip_x()</code>, <code>print(p)</code> prints <code>(3, -2)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    # ---- given: printing and drawing (do not change) ----\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def draw(self, ax, color=None):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=color or self.color, zorder=3)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def flip_x(self):\n        # write your code here\n\n    def flip_y(self):\n        # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- See it! (not graded) Remove the # in front of the lines below, then press Pre-check ----\n# import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n# fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n# ax.set_aspect('equal')\n# ax.axhline(0, color='lightgrey')\n# ax.axvline(0, color='lightgrey')\n# Point(3, 2).draw(ax, \"grey\")\n# p = Point(3, 2, \"red\")\n# p.flip_x()\n# p.draw(ax)\n# q = Point(3, 2, \"blue\")\n# q.flip_y()\n# q.draw(ax)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
