  {
   "xml_index": 5,
   "xml_name": "L11_005_Scaling A Point",
   "display_name": "Scaling A Point",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><b>Scaling</b> by a factor <code>k</code> multiplies both coordinates by <code>k</code>, moving the point <code>k</code> times further from the origin (towards it if <code>k</code> is between 0 and 1).</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the method <code>scale(k)</code>, which multiplies the point's <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> by <code>k</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>p = Point(2, 1)</code> and <code>p.scale(3)</code>, <code>print(p)</code> prints <code>(6, 3)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    # ---- given: printing and drawing (do not change) ----\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def draw(self, ax, color=None):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=color or self.color, zorder=3)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def flip_x(self):\n        self.y = -self.y        # mirror in the x-axis\n\n    def flip_y(self):\n        self.x = -self.x        # mirror in the y-axis\n\n    def rotate90(self):\n        # a quarter turn anticlockwise about the origin: (x, y) -> (-y, x)\n        self.x, self.y = -self.y, self.x\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- See it! (not graded) Remove the # in front of the lines below, then press Pre-check ----\n# import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n# fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n# ax.set_aspect('equal')\n# ax.axhline(0, color='lightgrey')\n# ax.axvline(0, color='lightgrey')\n# Point(2, 1).draw(ax, \"grey\")\n# p = Point(2, 1, \"red\")\n# p.scale(3)\n# p.draw(ax)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
