  {
   "xml_index": 6,
   "xml_name": "L11_006_Turning Around Another Point",
   "display_name": "Turning Around Another Point",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A method can <b>call other methods of the same object</b>, with <code>self.method(...)</code>. This lets us build a new operation from the ones we already have.</p>\n<p>To turn a point a quarter turn around another centre <code>(cx, cy)</code> (instead of the origin):</p>\n<ol><li>move it so that the centre is at the origin: <code>self.move(-cx, -cy)</code>;</li><li>turn it around the origin: <code>self.rotate90()</code>;</li><li>move it back: <code>self.move(cx, cy)</code>.</li></ol>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the method <code>rotate90_about(cx, cy)</code>, using <code>move</code> and <code>rotate90</code> as above.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>p = Point(3, 1)</code> and <code>p.rotate90_about(2, 1)</code>, <code>print(p)</code> prints <code>(2, 2)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    # ---- given: printing and drawing (do not change) ----\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def draw(self, ax, color=None):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=color or self.color, zorder=3)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def flip_x(self):\n        self.y = -self.y        # mirror in the x-axis\n\n    def flip_y(self):\n        self.x = -self.x        # mirror in the y-axis\n\n    def rotate90(self):\n        # a quarter turn anticlockwise about the origin: (x, y) -> (-y, x)\n        self.x, self.y = -self.y, self.x\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        self.x = self.x * k\n        self.y = self.y * k\n\n    def rotate90_about(self, cx, cy):\n        # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- See it! (not graded) Remove the # in front of the lines below, then press Pre-check ----\n# import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n# fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n# ax.set_aspect('equal')\n# ax.axhline(0, color='lightgrey')\n# ax.axvline(0, color='lightgrey')\n# Point(2, 1, \"black\").draw(ax)            # the centre\n# p = Point(3, 1, \"red\")\n# for i in range(4):\n#     p.draw(ax)\n#     p.rotate90_about(2, 1)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "p = Point(3, 1)\np.rotate90_about(2, 1)\nprint(p)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(2, 2)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "p = Point(5, 5)\np.rotate90_about(5, 5)\nprint(p)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(5, 5)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
