   "xml_index": 7,
   "xml_name": "L11_007_Distance Between Points",
   "display_name": "Distance Between Points",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A method can take <b>another object of the same class</b> as a parameter. Inside <code>p.distance_to(q)</code>, <code>self</code> is <code>p</code> and <code>other</code> is <code>q</code>.</p>\n<p>The distance between two points is <code>((x2 - x1)<b>2 + (y2 - y1)</b>2) ** 0.5</code> (Pythagoras).</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the method <code>distance_to(other)</code>, which returns the distance from this point to the point <code>other</code>, rounded to 2 decimal places with <code>round(value, 2)</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>Point(0, 0).distance_to(Point(3, 4))</code> returns <code>5.0</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    # ---- given: printing and drawing (do not change) ----\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def draw(self, ax, color=None):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=color or self.color, zorder=3)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def flip_x(self):\n        self.y = -self.y        # mirror in the x-axis\n\n    def flip_y(self):\n        self.x = -self.x        # mirror in the y-axis\n\n    def rotate90(self):\n        # a quarter turn anticlockwise about the origin: (x, y) -> (-y, x)\n        self.x, self.y = -self.y, self.x\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        self.x = self.x * k\n        self.y = self.y * k\n\n    def rotate90_about(self, cx, cy):\n        # move the centre to the origin, turn, and move back: three existing methods\n        self.move(-cx, -cy)\n        self.rotate90()\n        self.move(cx, cy)\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        # write your code here\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
