  {
   "xml_index": 13,
   "xml_name": "L11_013_Scaling And Turning A Triangle",
   "display_name": "Scaling And Turning A Triangle",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Two more transformations, each done corner by corner:</p>\n<ul><li><code>scale(k)</code>: scale every corner by <code>k</code> (the triangle grows <code>k</code> times, away from the origin);</li><li><code>rotate90()</code>: turn every corner a quarter turn around the origin.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the methods <code>scale(k)</code> and <code>rotate90()</code> of <code>Triangle</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>t = Triangle(Point(1, 1), Point(4, 1), Point(1, 3))</code> and <code>t.scale(2)</code>, <code>print(t)</code> prints <code>(2, 2) (8, 2) (2, 6)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    # ---- given: printing and drawing (do not change) ----\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def draw(self, ax, color=None):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=color or self.color, zorder=3)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def flip_x(self):\n        self.y = -self.y        # mirror in the x-axis\n\n    def flip_y(self):\n        self.x = -self.x        # mirror in the y-axis\n\n    def rotate90(self):\n        # a quarter turn anticlockwise about the origin: (x, y) -> (-y, x)\n        self.x, self.y = -self.y, self.x\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        self.x = self.x * k\n        self.y = self.y * k\n\n    def rotate90_about(self, cx, cy):\n        # move the centre to the origin, turn, and move back: three existing methods\n        self.move(-cx, -cy)\n        self.rotate90()\n        self.move(cx, cy)\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        return round(((other.x - self.x) ** 2 + (other.y - self.y) ** 2) ** 0.5, 2)\n\nclass Triangle:\n    def __init__(self, a, b, c, color=\"orange\"):\n        self.a = a              # three Point objects (the corners)\n        self.b = b\n        self.c = c\n        self.color = color\n\n    # ---- given: printing and drawing (do not change) ----\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.a) + \" \" + str(self.b) + \" \" + str(self.c)\n\n    def draw(self, ax, color=None):\n        xs = [self.a.x, self.b.x, self.c.x]\n        ys = [self.a.y, self.b.y, self.c.y]\n        ax.fill(xs, ys, color=color or self.color, alpha=0.5)\n\n    def corners(self):\n        return [self.a, self.b, self.c]\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        for p in self.corners():        # move every corner\n            p.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def flip_x(self):\n        for p in self.corners():\n            p.flip_x()\n\n    def flip_y(self):\n        for p in self.corners():\n            p.flip_y()\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        # write your code here\n\n    def rotate90(self):\n        # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- See it! (not graded) Remove the # in front of the lines below, then press Pre-check ----\n# import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n# fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n# ax.set_aspect('equal')\n# ax.axhline(0, color='lightgrey')\n# ax.axvline(0, color='lightgrey')\n# t = Triangle(Point(1, 1), Point(4, 1), Point(1, 3))\n# t.draw(ax, 'grey')\n# t.scale(2)\n# t.draw(ax)\n# for i in range(3):\n#     t.rotate90()\n#     t.draw(ax)\n",
