  {
   "xml_index": 17,
   "xml_name": "L11_017_A Pinwheel",
   "display_name": "A Pinwheel",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>To finish, use your classes to make a picture: a <b>pinwheel</b> of four triangles, each one a quarter turn further than the last.</p>\n<p>Plan: start with one triangle; for each of the four blades, add a <b>copy</b> of the current triangle to the scene, then turn the triangle a quarter turn for the next blade.</p>\n<p>Remove the <code>#</code> signs in the drawing block to see your pinwheel.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>make_pinwheel()</code>, which returns a <code>Scene</code> containing four triangles: the first is <code>Triangle(Point(0, 0), Point(4, 0), Point(4, 2))</code>, and each next one is the previous one turned a quarter turn around the origin (all four keep the default colour).</p>\n<p>For example, the second triangle of the scene prints as <code>(0, 0) (0, 4) (-2, 4)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    # ---- given: printing and drawing (do not change) ----\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def draw(self, ax, color=None):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=color or self.color, zorder=3)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def flip_x(self):\n        self.y = -self.y        # mirror in the x-axis\n\n    def flip_y(self):\n        self.x = -self.x        # mirror in the y-axis\n\n    def rotate90(self):\n        # a quarter turn anticlockwise about the origin: (x, y) -> (-y, x)\n        self.x, self.y = -self.y, self.x\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        self.x = self.x * k\n        self.y = self.y * k\n\n    def rotate90_about(self, cx, cy):\n        # move the centre to the origin, turn, and move back: three existing methods\n        self.move(-cx, -cy)\n        self.rotate90()\n        self.move(cx, cy)\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        return round(((other.x - self.x) ** 2 + (other.y - self.y) ** 2) ** 0.5, 2)\n\nclass Line:\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2, color=\"blue\"):\n        self.p1 = p1            # two Point objects\n        self.p2 = p2\n        self.color = color\n\n    # ---- given: printing and drawing (do not change) ----\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.p1) + \"-\" + str(self.p2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax, color=None):\n        ax.plot([self.p1.x, self.p2.x], [self.p1.y, self.p2.y], color=color or self.color)\n\n    def length(self):\n        return self.p1.distance_to(self.p2)     # ask a point to do the work\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.p1.move(dx, dy)                    # delegate to the two points\n        self.p2.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def rotate90(self):\n        self.p1.rotate90()\n        self.p2.rotate90()\n\nclass Triangle:\n    def __init__(self, a, b, c, color=\"orange\"):\n        self.a = a              # three Point objects (the corners)\n        self.b = b\n        self.c = c\n        self.color = color\n\n    # ---- given: printing and drawing (do not change) ----\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.a) + \" \" + str(self.b) + \" \" + str(self.c)\n\n    def draw(self, ax, color=None):\n        xs = [self.a.x, self.b.x, self.c.x]\n        ys = [self.a.y, self.b.y, self.c.y]\n        ax.fill(xs, ys, color=color or self.color, alpha=0.5)\n\n    def corners(self):\n        return [self.a, self.b, self.c]\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        for p in self.corners():        # move every corner\n            p.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def flip_x(self):\n        for p in self.corners():\n            p.flip_x()\n\n    def flip_y(self):\n        for p in self.corners():\n            p.flip_y()\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        for p in self.corners():\n            p.scale(k)\n\n    def rotate90(self):\n        for p in self.corners():\n            p.rotate90()\n\n    def copy(self):\n        # new Point objects, so changing the copy never changes the original\n        return Triangle(Point(self.a.x, self.a.y), Point(self.b.x, self.b.y),\n                        Point(self.c.x, self.c.y), self.color)\n\nclass Scene:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.shapes = []\n\n    # ---- given: drawing (do not change) ----\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        for s in self.shapes:\n            s.draw(ax)                # every shape draws itself\n\n    def add(self, shape):\n        self.shapes.append(shape)\n\n    def move_all(self, dx, dy):\n        for s in self.shapes:\n            s.move(dx, dy)            # each shape uses its own move()\n\n    def rotate_all(self):\n        for s in self.shapes:\n            s.rotate90()\n\n\ndef make_pinwheel():\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- See it! (not graded) Remove the # in front of the lines below, then press Pre-check ----\n# import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n# fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n# ax.set_aspect('equal')\n# ax.axhline(0, color='lightgrey')\n# ax.axvline(0, color='lightgrey')\n# make_pinwheel().draw(ax)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "s = make_pinwheel()\nprint(len(s.shapes))\nprint(s.shapes[1])",
     "stdin": "",
